%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Domestic Terrorism
  crisisName: Domestic Terrorism
  resolutionSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 50a43b9915dc7014080a8f1bca2dd5aa, type: 3}
  crisisStartSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: fc938e1eb80e1884d8a328a6ea750f5f, type: 3}
  obviousWarningSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 563ed8c2154a8fa42a576650f4375e90, type: 3}
  ominousWarningSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 46225c091dfaa4a4f877ba39f4ab36b8, type: 3}
  ominousWarningText: "Warnings are multiplying. Security services have intercepted threatening messages, unexplained financial transfers, suspicious movements around vulnerable infrastructure, and communications between individuals already connected to extremist networks. Some messages speak of retaliation, others of independence, religious struggle, political revenge, or resistance to the state, but authorities cannot yet determine which threats are genuine and which are intended only to spread fear. Local officials request additional security around transport hubs, government buildings, utilities, and crowded public spaces. Rumors circulate faster than verified information, increasing tension in communities already divided by political or social grievances. No attack has yet occurred. Intelligence officers increasingly believe that someone is preparing one."
  obviousWarningText: "Security services have identified an active plot. Surveillance and intercepted communications indicate that several teams may already be moving toward possible targets, though authorities cannot determine whether every location under threat has been discovered. Transport hubs close with little warning, government facilities restrict access, and emergency units deploy around power stations, communications centers, and other critical infrastructure. Police checkpoints appear across affected cities while investigators race to locate weapons, explosives, safe houses, or accomplices before the operation begins. The sudden security measures themselves spread fear, disrupting ordinary life even before violence occurs. The threat is no longer theoretical. Multiple targets may already be in danger."
  crisisStartText: "The plot has become an active campaign of violence. Extremist cells operating inside our territory are now attempting to sabotage infrastructure, disrupt public life, and strike at vulnerable cities rather than confront the state as a conventional army. Terrorist forces may emerge in areas already suffering severe political, religious, separatist, or social grievances, and their attacks can damage buildings and improvements if allowed to operate freely. Security forces can hunt down the cells, protect likely targets, or work to reduce the instability from which the movement draws support. A powerful army abroad means little if roads, utilities, and communities at home cannot be protected. The battlefield is now inside our own cities."
  resolutionText: "The cells have been broken. Security forces have rooted out the networks behind the campaign of violence, whether through arrests, raids, or the slower work of addressing the grievances that gave the movement its strength. Checkpoints are dismantled, transport hubs reopen, and the heightened patrols that once unsettled daily life gradually fade from the streets. Investigators continue tracing the surviving threads of the conspiracy, aware that a single missed cell could reignite the danger. Damaged buildings are repaired, and the fear that once accompanied every crowded gathering slowly recedes. The immediate threat has passed. The conditions that created it will require more than security forces to resolve."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 20
  useAgeWindow: 1
  minimumAge: 14
  maximumAge: 17
  mechanic: 12
  minimumRiskScore: 35
  scope: 1
